# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: Other | Scene: MariusPath

translate es strings:

    old "When Sarah woke the next morning, the day unfolded, same as before."
    new "Cuando Sarah se despertó la mañana siguiente, el día transcurrió igual que antes."

    old "She rose with the others, made breakfast, send Marius on his way early, and took the house work."
    new "Se levantó con los demás, preparó el desayuno, despidió a Marius temprano y se encargó de las tareas del hogar."

    old "Sarah was surprised to learn that even in so small a household, the daily work required to maintain it was almost a full job."
    new "Sarah se sorprendió al descubrir que incluso en una casa tan pequeña, el trabajo diario necesario para mantenerla era casi un empleo completo."

    old "After finishing up the remainder of the laundry that she had not been able to get to the day before, she took to cleaning up inside the home."
    new "Después de terminar con el resto del lavado que no había podido hacer el día anterior, se puso a limpiar el interior de la casa."

    old "The two men had lived rather practically before she arrived, and cleanliness was a distant consideration."
    new "Los dos hombres habían vivido bastante pragmáticamente antes de su llegada, y la limpieza era una consideración lejana."

    old "Sarah imagined that now she was here, at the very least, she could add a feminine touch."
    new "Sarah imaginaba que, al menos ahora que estaba allí, podría aportar un toque femenino."

    old "She headed back into the yard and began to walk the perimeter, marked by the ramshackle fence."
    new "Salió de nuevo al patio y comenzó a recorrer el perímetro, delimitado por la valla precaria."

    old "It was a sizeable plot, she realized."
    new "Era una parcela considerable, lo comprendió."

    old "A large oak tree, some small garden plots for various vegetables. A dilapidated barn that housed a few animals."
    new "Un roble enorme, algunos lechos de huerta para diversas verduras. Un establo derruido que alojaba a unos pocos animales."

    old "Animals and Marius' father, Alfred."
    new "Animales y el padre de Marius, Alfred."

    old "An animal of a different sort, she concluded."
    new "Un animal de otra especie, concluyó."

    old "Out near the far eastern edge of the plot, she found a patch of flowers, growing in between the fence posts."
    new "Al borde oriental del terreno, encontró un grupo de flores creciendo entre los postes de la cerca."

    old "Kneeling down, Sarah carefully studied the flowers."
    new "Arrodillada, Sarah examinó cuidadosamente las flores."

    old "In castle Reinmeer, she had always loved flowers and plants. The royal garden had been especially precious to her."
    new "En el castillo Reinmeer, siempre había amado las flores y las plantas. El jardín real había sido especialmente preciado para ella."

    old "But now it struck her how different these flowers were."
    new "Pero ahora le pareció cuán diferentes eran estas flores."

    old "Here they lacked the disciplined hands of the dozen gardeners that carefully managed and treated each specimen."
    new "Aquí carecían de las manos disciplinadas de los doce jardineros que cuidaban y trataban cada ejemplar."

    old "Instead, they grew wildly and chaotically."
    new "En cambio, crecieron salvajemente y de forma caótica."

    old "But in a sense, they had their own beauty because of it."
    new "Pero en cierto sentido, tenían su propia belleza debido a ello."

    old "Closer to how nature had intended for them to be."
    new "Más cerca de cómo la naturaleza había pretendido que fueran."

    old "More full of life, rather than the sterile world of the castle."
    new "Más llena de vida, en lugar del mundo estéril del castillo."

    old "She smiled as she leaned forward to pluck a few."
    new "Sonrió mientras se inclinaba hacia adelante para arrancar algunas."

    old "No more than she needed."
    new "No más de lo que necesitaba."

    old "When she returned to the house, she placed them in a vase on the table and went back to the work."
    new "Cuando regresó a la casa, los colocó en un jarrón sobre la mesa y volvió a su trabajo."

    old "Sweeping, cleaning, preparing dinner."
    new "Barrer, limpiar, preparar la cena."

    old "Time, and the day, had a way of slipping through her fingers."
    new "El tiempo y el día tenían la costumbre de deslizarse entre sus dedos."

    old "Still working, Sarah idely looked up and saw Marius approach through the window."
    new "Sigue trabajando, Sarah miró hacia arriba con curiosidad y vio a Marius acercarse por la ventana."

    old "She rushed out to meet him."
    new "Se precipitó a encontrarse con él."

    old "The sun low and golden behind him, it marked his arrival almost as certainly as any clock would."
    new "El sol, bajo y dorado a sus espaldas, marcó su llegada casi con la certeza de cualquier reloj."

    old "He smiled and waved at her."
    new "Sonrió y le hizo un gesto con la mano."

    old "She did the same back."
    new "Ella hizo lo mismo de vuelta."

    old "Hey!"
    new "¡Hola!"

    old "Sarah noticed the heavy stains of sweat on his clothes. He had worked himself to the bone again."
    new "Sarah notó las manchas pesadas de sudor en su ropa. Había trabajado hasta el hueso otra vez."

    old "Marius!"
    new "¡Marius!"

    old "What?"
    new "¿Qué?"

    old "You work too hard!"
    new "¡Trabajas demasiado!"

    old "He laughed as he stopped walking."
    new "Rió al detenerse."

    old "This?"
    new "¿Esto?"

    old "He padded his clothes."
    new "Ladeó su ropa."

    old "This is nothing. I'm used to it."
    new "Esto es nada. Ya estoy acostumbrado a esto."

    old "Still. It can't be healthy to work this hard, every day."
    new "Aún así. No puede ser saludable trabajar tan duro todos los días."

    old "You need to take care of yourself too. Not just everyone else."
    new "Tú también necesitas cuidar de ti misma. No solo a los demás."

    old "Marius nodded and smiled."
    new "Marius asintió y sonrió."

    old "You're right."
    new "Tienes razón."

    old "But once the harvest season is over, things will get easier."
    new "Pero una vez que termine la cosecha, las cosas se pondrán más fáciles."

    old "Sarah nodded. She just hoped it was true, for his sake."
    new "Sarah asintió. Solo esperaba que fuera cierto, por su bien."

    old "Come in, I've got dinner ready."
    new "Entra, ya tengo la cena lista."

    old "Marius gestured at the horizon."
    new "Marius señaló el horizonte."

    old "Why eat inside when we got a view like this?"
    new "¿Por qué comer dentro cuando tenemos una vista como esta?"

    old "Sarah hadn't even considered the option."
    new "Sarah ni siquiera había considerado esa opción."

    old "Oh...you're right."
    new "Oh...tienes razón."

    old "You get the food, we'll eat it by the oak tree. Soun good."
    new "Tú te encargas de la comida, y comeremos bajo el roble. Suena bien."

    old "Sarah nodded and excitedly retrieved the food."
    new "Sarah asintió y con entusiasmo recogió la comida."

    old "When she approached the large oak tree, she saw Marius was already sitting in the alcove."
    new "Cuando se acercó al gran roble, vio que Marius ya estaba sentado en la hornacina."

    old "The large tree had roots that wandered and twisted about, forming almost natural places to take rest in."
    new "El gran árbol tenía raíces que se adentraban y enredaban, formando casi lugares naturales para descansar."

    old "Sarah sat down besides Marius on one of the particularly large roots."
    new "Sarah se sentó al lado de Marius en una de las raíces particularmente grandes."

    old "Here."
    new "Aquí."

    old "She handed him the bowl of stew."
    new "Le entregó el cuenco de estofado."

    old "Eagerly he took it."
    new "Con ansia lo tomó."

    old "Thanks, I'm starving."
    new "Gracias, estoy muerto de hambre."

    old "He looked caught out again."
    new "Quedó atrapado otra vez."

    old "You work that hard and you don't even eat a proper lunch?"
    new "¿Trabajas tan duro y ni siquiera comes un almuerzo decente?"

    old "I mean...I'm out so early, I just never..."
    new "I mean... salgo tan temprano que nunca..."

    old "Just, let me do it, okay?"
    new "Solo déjame hacerlo, ¿vale?"

    old "I'll make you a lunch you can take out to the field when you go to work."
    new "Haré un almuerzo para que lo lleves al campo cuando vayas a trabajar."

    old "Really?"
    new "¿De verdad?"

    old "She saw a strange flicker in his eyes."
    new "Vio un extraño parpadeo en sus ojos."

    old "Of course. It's no trouble for me. I wake early with you anyway."
    new "Claro, no es ningún problema para mí. Me levanto temprano contigo de todos modos."

    old "Gosh, Sarah...you really are a life saver."
    new "¡Joder, Sarah... realmente eres un salvavidas."

    old "She blushed and smiled."
    new "Se sonrojó y sonrió."

    old "Don't worry. It's the least I can do for what you've given me."
    new "No te preocupes. Es lo menos que puedo hacer por todo lo que me has dado."

    old "Marius looked back at the house."
    new "Marius volvió la mirada hacia la casa."

    old "Oh, yeah..."
    new "Oh, sí..."

    old "How are you liking it so far, anyway?"
    new "¿Y hasta ahora, qué te parece?"

    old "It's great. Really. This town...I think it's exactly what I had been looking for."
    new "Es genial. De verdad. Este pueblo... creo que es exactamente lo que estaba buscando."

    old "Marius looked off into the distance."
    new "Marius miró hacia el horizonte."

    old "You know, Sarah...you don't have to go any time soon."
    new "Sabes, Sarah... no tienes que irte pronto."

    old "I mean...you don't have to stay if you don't want to, obviously, but...I don't mind you staying over."
    new "Digo... no tienes que quedarte si no quieres, obviamente, pero... no me importa que te quedes a pasar la noche."

    old "Sarah smiled at him, and in his face she could see there wasn't a word he didn't mean."
    new "Sarah sonrió, y en su rostro pude ver que no había palabra que no quisiera decir."

    old "Thank you, Marius. You've really been so kind to me."
    new "Gracias, Marius. Has sido tan amable conmigo."

    old "The two of them continued to eat as they talked about their lives."
    new "Los dos continuaron comiendo mientras hablaban de sus vidas."

    old "Marius spoke openly about growing up in Gallow's Creek."
    new "Marius habló abiertamente sobre su crecimiento en Gallow's Creek."

    old "Sarah, for her part, spoke it half veiled truths, trying to be as honest as she could be with him."
    new "Sarah, por su parte, lo dijo a medias, tratando de ser tan honesta con él como pudo."

    old "Marius was hardly someone that would use the information about her life against her."
    new "Marius no era precisamente el tipo que utilizaría la información sobre su vida en su contra."

    old "But she feared what it might do to their relationship."
    new "Pero temía lo que podría hacer con su relación."

    old "Feared that if he knew she had been a Princess, he might grow distant with her."
    new "Teme que si él supiera que ella había sido una Princesa, podría alejarse de ella."

    old "Just when she yearned for closeness."
    new "Justo cuando ansiaba cercanía."

    old "Marius' voice was soft, tender."
    new "La voz de Marius era suave y tierna."

    old "In town..."
    new "En la ciudad..."

    old "He spoke slowly, as if considering every word."
    new "Hablaba despacio, como si estuviera ponderando cada palabra."

    old "In town, after the harvest comes in..."
    new "En el pueblo, después de la cosecha..."

    old "Well, there is usually a harvest festival. People make food, music...dance."
    new "Bueno, usualmente hay una fiesta de la cosecha. La gente prepara comida, música... baila."

    old "If you'd like...I could take you there?"
    new "Si lo deseas... podría llevarte allí?"

    old "I mean, show you around town. It would be a great chance to get to meet everyone."
    new "I mean, mostrarte la ciudad. Sería una gran oportunidad para conocer a todo el mundo."

    old "Sarah saw the desperation in his eyes."
    new "Sarah vio la desesperación en sus ojos."

    old "He was not a man used to being vulnerable."
    new "No era un hombre acostumbrado a la vulnerabilidad."

    old "Of course I'll go with you."
    new "Por supuesto que iré contigo."

    old "It sounds like fun."
    new "Suena divertido."

    old "Besides, I love to dance."
    new "Además, adoro bailar."

    old "Marius suddenly had a panicked expression on his face."
    new "De repente, Marius tuvo una expresión de terror en su rostro."

    old "I...I can't dance..."
    new "Yo... no sé bailar..."

    old "She reached over and placed one hand on his arm."
    new "Se estiró y colocó una mano en su brazo."

    old "You show me around town. I'll show you how to dance."
    new "Me muestras el pueblo y yo te enseño a bailar."

    old "Laughing, the two of them continued to eat together and tell stories of their lives."
    new "Riendo, los dos continuaron comiendo juntos y contándose historias de sus vidas."

    old "It was a long time befor either of them realized how dark it had gotten."
    new "Fue mucho tiempo antes de que ninguno de los dos se diera cuenta de qué tan oscuro había llegado a ser."

    old "They gathered up their plates and headed inside."
    new "Reunieron sus platos y entraron."

    old "Marius motioned at the flowers on the table."
    new "Marius señaló las flores sobre la mesa."

    old "Did you do that?"
    new "¿Lo hiciste?"

    old "You don't like them?"
    new "¿No te gustan?"

    old "No...they're great..."
    new "No... son grandes..."

    old "There was something odd in his voice, but Sarah couldn't say what."
    new "Había algo extraño en su voz, pero Sarah no podía decir qué."

    old "The two parted ways, each retiring to their own room."
    new "Los dos se separaron, retirándose cada uno a su propia habitación."

    old "Sarah laid down in her bed and looked up at the ceiling."
    new "Sarah se recostó en su cama y miró hacia el techo."

    old "In her mind, she replayed her conversation with Marius, over and over again, until she fell asleep."
    new "En su mente, repitió su conversación con Marius una y otra vez, hasta que se durmió."

    old "Days came and went, each much the same."
    new "Pasaron días y pasaron, cada uno muy parecido al anterior."

    old "Sarah settled into a comfortable pace."
    new "Sarah se acomodó a un ritmo cómodo."

    old "Each day she imagined she was getting just a little better at all the house work."
    new "Cada día imaginaba que se estaba volviendo un poco más hábil en todo el trabajo del hogar."

    old "And the house showed the results of her efforts."
    new "Y la casa mostraba los resultados de sus esfuerzos."

    old "The practical room where people slept had slowly become a home."
    new "La habitación práctica donde la gente dormía había ido convirtiéndose lentamente en un hogar."

    old "Nearly a week had gone by when Marius reminded her that the harvest festival was in only a few days."
    new "Casi una semana había transcurrido cuando Marius le recordó que la fiesta de la cosecha era en solo unos días."

    old "The festival had almost slipped her minds."
    new "El festival casi se le había escapado de la mente."

    old "Sarah spend what little free time she had, sowing a few adjustments to her dress."
    new "Sarah aprovechó el poco tiempo libre que tenía para realizar unos pequeños ajustes a su vestido."

    old "On the night itself, she looked into the window, which was as close as they had to a mirror."
    new "En la noche misma, miró por la ventana, que era tan cercana como podían tener a un espejo."

    old "Staring back at her was the perfect reflection of a farm girl."
    new "De vuelta mirándola estaba la imagen perfecta de una chica del campo."

    old "Already so distant from the Princess she had long been."
    new "Ya tan distante de la Princesa que siempre había sido."

    old "How quick life re-made her, she wondered."
    new "¿A qué velocidad la vida la había reconstruido, se preguntó."

    old "Sarah plucked on the flowers from the vase."
    new "Sarah arrancó las flores del jarrón."

    old "This had been Marius' favorite."
    new "Esta había sido el favorito de Marius."

    old "Carefully, she placed into the strands of her hair, near her ear."
    new "Con cuidado, colocó algo entre las hebras de su cabello, cerca de su oreja."

    old "She smiled at herself. Proud."
    new "Sonrió a sí misma. Orgullosa."

    old "Just then, the door flew open and Marius stumbled in."
    new "Justo entonces, la puerta se abrió de golpe y Marius entró tambaleándose."

    old "When he saw her, his jaw dropped."
    new "Cuando la vio, su mandíbula cayó."

    old "You..."
    new "Tú..."

    old "You look incredible..."
    new "Te ves increíble..."

    old "In court, nobles played endless games of hiding their emotions and their intentions."
    new "En la corte, los nobles jugaban interminables juegos de ocultar sus emociones y sus intenciones."

    old "Marius just said whatever laid on his heart."
    new "Marius dijo simplemente lo que le venía a la mente."

    old "I thought I'd put in a little extra effort for the festival."
    new "Pensé que pondría un poco más de empeño para el festival."

    old "Are you ready?"
    new "¿Estás lista?"

    old "But now I feel bad. I'm underdress."
    new "Pero ahora me siento mal. Estoy desvestido."

    old "Sarah walked up to him and looped her arm into his."
    new "Sarah se acercó a él y le enlazó el brazo."

    old "She felt his body jolt from the slight touch of their skin."
    new "Sintió cómo el cuerpo de él se estremecía ante el leve contacto de su piel."

    old "You look great."
    new "Te ves increíble."

    old "Together, the two of them left the house and began to make their way towards the town's center."
    new "Juntos, los dos salieron de la casa y comenzaron a dirigirse hacia el centro del pueblo."

    old "Even from a distance, the many lights and people gathered, blazed in the dark of night like a bonfire."
    new "Incluso desde lejos, las muchas luces y la gente reunida brillaban en la oscuridad de la noche como un fuego de hoguera."

    old "As they came closer, she could hear the growing sounds of music and laughing."
    new "A medida que se acercaban, pudo oír los crecientes sonidos de música y risas."

    old "It sounds fun."
    new "Suena divertido."

    old "Well, it's the best we can do, you know."
    new "Bueno, es lo mejor que podemos hacer, ¿sabes?"

    old "I'm sure you're used to bigger things."
    new "Estoy seguro de que estás acostumbrada a cosas mayores."

    old "Sarah patted his arm."
    new "Sarah le acarició el brazo."

    old "Maybe, but I never had such good company."
    new "Quizás, pero nunca tuve compañía tan buena."

    old "She saw him blush at her remark."
    new "Vio que él se ruborizó ante su comentario."

    old "As they ventured further into the town, Sarah saw a crowd begin to form."
    new "A medida que avanzaban más profundo en el pueblo, Sarah vio cómo comenzaba a formarse una multitud."

    old "Compared to where she had grown up in Rosanna, Gallow's Creek was tiny."
    new "En comparación con el lugar donde había crecido en Rosanna, Gallow's Creek era diminuto."

    old "But all packed together for the festival, even this small town suddenly seemed big."
    new "Pero todos amontonados para el festival, incluso este pequeño pueblo pareció de repente enorme."

    old "Sarah watched as Marius greeted almost all of them as they walked through the town."
    new "Sarah observó cómo Marius saludaba a casi todos ellos mientras caminaban por el pueblo."

    old "Wow, you sure know a lot of people..."
    new "Vaya, seguro que conoces a mucha gente..."

    old "Born here. Grew up here. Never gonna leave."
    new "Nacido aquí. Crecido aquí. Nunca voy a irme."

    old "You get to know a place, I guess."
    new "Supongo que te das cuenta del lugar."

    old "Sarah saw his eyes glitter."
    new "Sarah vio cómo sus ojos brillaban."

    old "In all her life, just about everyone she ever met was busy trying to get somewhere else."
    new "En toda su vida, casi todos los que había conocido se habían dedicado a tratar de llegar a otra parte."

    old "Somewhere else in life, be it station or place."
    new "En algún otro lugar de la vida, sea estación o sitio."

    old "But not him."
    new "Pero no él."

    old "All this time, he had been here, content with what he had, rather than losing himself in a struggle to get more."
    new "Todo este tiempo, él había estado aquí, conforme con lo que tenía, en lugar de perderse luchando por conseguir más."

    old "He didn't want mansions or mountains of gold."
    new "No quería mansiones ni montañas de oro."

    old "If you offered him a crown, he'd probably hand it back."
    new "Si le ofrecieras una corona, probablemente se la devolvería."

    old "He was perfectly happy where he was."
    new "Estaba perfectamente feliz donde estaba."

    old "I'm kind of jealous."
    new "Estoy un poco celosa."

    old "She decided to be honest with him, or at least as much as she could be."
    new "Decidió ser honesta con él, o al menos tanto como pudiera."

    old "Jealous?"
    new "¿Celosa?"

    old "You seem so...at home."
    new "Pareces tan... como en casa."

    old "Like you're exactly where you're supposed to be."
    new "Como si estuvieras exactamente donde debías estar."

    old "I suppose."
    new "Supongo."

    old "I mean, I love every part of this land. I've worked it summer after summer."
    new "Digo, amo cada parte de esta tierra. La he trabajado verano tras verano."

    old "And the people are good. Decent."
    new "Y la gente es buena. Decente."

    old "But it's not all perfect, trust me."
    new "Pero no todo es perfecto, créeme."

    old "Sarah frowned as they walked further through the festival."
    new "Sarah frunció el ceño mientras avanzaban por la feria."

    old "Forget it."
    new "Déjalo."

    old "His voice was suddenly brisk."
    new "Su voz se tornó repentinamente seca."

    old "Sarah pulled at his arm, forcing him to stop."
    new "Sarah tiró de su brazo, obligándolo a detenerse."

    old "No. Tell me what you meant."
    new "No. Dime qué querías decir."

    old "Marius suddenly looked away, as if afraid of making eye contact."
    new "Marius desvió bruscamente la mirada, como si temiera establecer contacto visual."

    old "It's just..."
    new "Es solo..."

    old "This town is small. There aren't a lot of people."
    new "Este pueblo es pequeño. No hay mucha gente."

    old "That's good...but it's also..."
    new "Eso es bueno... pero también es..."

    old "I don't know...it can be lonely."
    new "No lo sé... puede ser solitario."

    old "Sarah saw the hurt in his eyes."
    new "Sarah vio el dolor en sus ojos."

    old "Lonely...I can understand that."
    new "Solitaria... puedo entender eso."

    old "It's just...it didn't used to be like that."
    new "Solo que... ya no era así antes."

    old "Before, when it was me, my dad and my mom, it was all perfect."
    new "Antes, cuando era yo, mi papá y mi mamá, todo era perfecto."

    old "And I always dreamed of having something like that myself, you know, a family?"
    new "Y yo siempre soñé con tener algo así también, ¿sabes? Una familia."

    old "But after mom died, my dad he...I don't know, he turned colder."
    new "Pero después de que mamá murió, mi papá él... no sé, se volvió más frío."

    old "And as he got older, I had to pick up more of the work."
    new "Y conforme él envejecía, tuve que asumir más del trabajo."

    old "But it was just enough to keep us fed and keep the house over our head."
    new "Pero era suficiente para mantenernos alimentados y mantener el techo sobre nuestras cabezas."

    old "I was focussed on surviving."
    new "Estaba concentrado en sobrevivir."

    old "So by the time I looked up and thought about a family of my own, most of the women in town had already settled."
    new "Así que cuando miré hacia arriba y pensé en tener mi propia familia, la mayoría de las mujeres del pueblo ya se habían establecido."

    old "And in this place, if you miss the boat...well, there ain't much second chances."
    new "Y en este lugar, si te pierdes el barco... bueno, no hay muchas segundas oportunidades."

    old "I think I can understand."
    new "Creo que puedo entender."

    old "I've been the same, in a lot of ways."
    new "He sido igual en muchos aspectos."

    old "Running. Surviving. Always so busy that I hardly have time to think of anything else."
    new "Corriendo. Sobreviviendo. Siempre tan ocupada que apenas tengo tiempo para pensar en otra cosa."

    old "I guess...if you keep that up for too long...you're always so focussed on the day to day, you forget to think about the bigger picture."
    new "Supongo... si sigues así por mucho tiempo... siempre estás tan enfocado en lo cotidiano que olvidas pensar en el panorama general."

    old "Exactly!"
    new "¡Exacto!"

    old "Gods, I was so afraid of telling you this."
    new "Dioses, tenía tanto miedo de decirte esto."

    old "Why would you be afraid?"
    new "¿Por qué tendrías que tener miedo?"

    old "Well...I thought you'd think poorly of me. That I offered you a place to stay, just because you're..."
    new "Bueno... pensé que me juzgarías mal. Que te ofreciera un lugar para quedarte, solo porque eres..."

    old "He stumbled on the last few words."
    new "Tardó en pronunciar las últimas palabras."

    old "Because what?"
    new "¿Por qué?"

    old "Because you're so pretty."
    new "Porque eres tan guapa."

    old "Sarah blushed at his sudden honesty."
    new "Sarah se ruborizó ante su repentina honestidad."

    old "She wasn't a fool. She knew how he looked at her."
    new "No era una tonta. Sabía cómo la miraba."

    old "But with him, she didn't mind as much."
    new "Pero con él, no le importaba tanto."

    old "Most men had eyes that were filled with malice and lust."
    new "La mayoría de los hombres tenían ojos llenos de maldad y lujuria."

    old "His were love."
    new "Los suyos eran amores."

    old "She reached out and touched his arm."
    new "Extendió la mano y tocó su brazo."

    old "With her fingers, she could feel the hard surface of his skin, muscled from a life of working the land."
    new "Con los dedos, podía sentir la superficie dura de su piel, musculada por una vida trabajando la tierra."

    old "Don't worry, Marius."
    new "No te preocupes, Marius."

    old "I could never think poorly of you."
    new "Nunca podría pensar mal de ti."

    old "You've shown me a kindness when nobody else will."
    new "Me has mostrado un acto de bondad cuando nadie más lo haría."

    old "I'll always be grateful for that."
    new "Siempre estaré agradecida por eso."

    old "He smiled at her again, with all the same genuine intent that defined him."
    new "Sonrió de nuevo a ella, con toda la misma intención genuina que lo definía."

    old "And Sarah felt a spark of something in her chest."
    new "Y Sarah sintió un destello de algo en su pecho."

    old "Together, the two of them continued to explore the festival."
    new "Juntos, los dos continuaron explorando la fiesta."

    old "One of the families from a nearby farmstead had a stand where they were frying something."
    new "Una de las familias de una granja cercana tenía un puesto donde estaban freyendo algo."

    old "Sarah lingered near the stand for a moment."
    new "Sarah se quedó un momento cerca del atril."

    old "You want one?"
    new "¿Quieres una?"

    old "Oh, no don't worry about it. I don't have any money."
    new "Oh, no, no te preocupes. No tengo dinero."

    old "Before she could even properly refute him, Marius had already reached into his pocket and pulled out a few coins."
    new "Antes de que siquiera pudiera refutarlo debidamente, Marius ya había metido la mano en su bolsillo y sacado unas pocas monedas."

    old "He handed the money to the stall owners, and a minute later, they received the fried food."
    new "Él entregó el dinero a los dueños de la parada, y un minuto después, recibieron la comida frita."

    old "They continued to explore the festival ground together whilst eating."
    new "Continuaron explorando el terreno del festival mientras comían."

    old "Wow, this is really good."
    new "¡Wow, esto es realmente bueno."

    old "Yeah, I used to be crazy about them."
    new "Sí, solía estar loco por ellos."

    old "When I worked my first season on the land, I had so much money I didn't know what to do with myself."
    new "Cuando trabajé mi primera temporada en la tierra, tenía tanto dinero que no sabía qué hacer conmigo mismo."

    old "I bought like two dozen of those things and ate them all."
    new "Compré como dos docenas de esas cosas y me las comí todas."

    old "Spend the next morning paying for it."
    new "Pasemos la mañana siguiente pagando por eso."

    old "Oh no!"
    new "¡Oh no!"

    old "Sarah laughed along with him."
    new "Sarah rió con él."

    old "It's true."
    new "Es cierto."

    old "Couldn't eat the things for a few years after that."
    new "No pudo comer esas cosas durante unos años después de eso."

    old "Sarah took another bite and pledged to only eat the one."
    new "Sarah tomó otra mordida y se comprometió a comer solo una."

    old "Thank you again, for buying me one."
    new "Gracias otra vez por comprármela."

    old "Sarah pointed towards a nearby log."
    new "Sarah señaló hacia un tronco cercano."

    old "You mind if we take a break? My feet are killing me."
    new "¿Te importa si tomamos un descanso? Me están matando los pies."

    old "Together, the two of them sat down on the log, a small distance away from the festival."
    new "Juntos, los dos se sentaron en el tronco, a poca distancia del festival."

    old "You like it so far?"
    new "¿Te gusta hasta ahora?"

    old "It's really fun."
    new "Es realmente divertido."

    old "I think I needed something like that."
    new "Creo que necesitaba algo así."

    old "It's not that you and your dad haven't been great for taking me in, you have..."
    new "No es que tú y tu padre no habéis sido geniales por darme cobijo, lo hacéis..."

    old "But that house can feel a little small. I think I needed to see some more people."
    new "Pero esa casa puede sentirse un poco pequeña. Creo que necesitaba ver a más gente."

    old "You think it feels small after a few days? Try a few years."
    new "¿Crees que se siente pequeño después de unos días? Prueba con varios años."

    old "Sarah frowned. It was the first time she had heard a negative word coming out of his mouth."
    new "Sarah frunció el ceño. Era la primera vez que escuchaba una palabra negativa salir de su boca."

    old "Oh, I thought you liked it."
    new "Oh, pensé que te gustaba."

    old "Marius looked at the festival. Right on the edge here, it felt like they were a part of it, and apart from it, at the same time."
    new "Marius observó la fiesta con curiosidad. Justo aquí, al borde de todo, sentía que eran parte de ella y, a la vez, extraños a ella."

    old "It's fine."
    new "Está bien."

    old "I mean, it is, really."
    new "Es decir, sí lo es, de verdad."

    old "But sometimes I feel like..."
    new "Pero a veces siento como..."

    old "Gods, I ain't none for words and stuff."
    new "Dios, no tengo paciencia para las tonterías."

    old "I just, I feel like I should be movin on to somethin, I don't know."
    new "Solo siento que debería estar avanzando hacia algo más, no sé."

    old "Sarah nodded and placed her hand on his arm."
    new "Sarah asintió y colocó su mano en su brazo."

    old "I understand, Marius. I really do."
    new "Entiendo, Marius. De verdad."

    old "You do?"
    new "¿Lo haces?"

    old "You're a good son. You took care for your dad after your mother passed."
    new "Eres un buen hijo. Te cuidaste de tu padre después de que tu madre falleció."

    old "But that's surviving, it's not living."
    new "Pero eso es sobrevivir, no vivir."

    old "You want something more to live for. I get that."
    new "Quieres algo más en qué vivir, lo entiendo."

    old "That's exactly it..."
    new "Eso es exactamente lo que quería decir..."

    old "Gods...you're so easy to talk to."
    new "Dioses... eres tan fácil de hablar con."

    old "He sighed and looked at the sky."
    new "Suspiró y miró al cielo."

    old "Sometimes I think the world is so big out there, and all I seen of it are these fields, ya know?"
    new "A veces pienso que el mundo es tan grande allá afuera, y todo lo que he visto de él son estos campos, ¿sabes?"

    old "Sarah looked at the sky herself."
    new "Sarah miró al cielo por sí misma."

    old "But I've seen plenty of the world. Too much of it already."
    new "Pero he visto bastante del mundo. Demasiado de él ya."

    old "It's a big world, but it's filled with horrid people, and not all that much worth seeing."
    new "Es un mundo grande, pero está lleno de gente horrible y no hay mucho que ver."

    old "A silence lingered for a moment."
    new "Narrador"

    old "That sounds pretty bleak."
    new "Suena bastante sombrío."

    old "I'm sorry. I didn't want to sound so gloomy."
    new "Lo siento. No quise sonar tan sombría."

    old "I'm really having a great time with you tonight."
    new "Me estoy pasando un momento increíble contigo esta noche."

    old "I'm having a great time with you as well, Sarah."
    new "Yo también lo estoy pasando en grande contigo, Sarah."

    old "He leaned a little closer."
    new "Se inclinó un poco más cerca."

    old "And Sarah leaned a little closer to him."
    new "Y Sarah se inclinó un poco más hacia él."

    old "Shoulder to shoulder, the two of them sat in a comfortable silence."
    new "De hombro con hombro, los dos se sentaron en un silencio cómodo."

    old "Maybe we both got it wrong."
    new "Quizás ambos nos equivocamos."

    old "How you figure."
    new "¿Cómo lo calculas."

    old "Maybe it's not abouting seeing the whole world, or seeing nothing of it."
    new "Quizás no se trata de ver el mundo entero, o de no verlo en absoluto."

    old "Maybe...between us, there's a balance."
    new "Quizás... entre nosotros, hay un equilibrio."

    old "A bit of the good of both."
    new "Un poco del bueno de ambos."

    old "I'd like that."
    new "Me gustaría eso."

    old "Sarah turned her face up and looked at him."
    new "Sarah levantó la cara y lo miró."

    old "His kind eyes drew her closer, without even realizing it."
    new "Sus ojos amables la atraían más cerca, sin darse cuenta."

    old "Sarah, I-"
    new "Sarah, yo—"

    old "She leaned forward and planted her lips on his."
    new "Se inclinó hacia adelante y colocó sus labios sobre los suyos."

    old "And he returned her passions with a pent-up desire of his own."
    new "Y devolvió sus pasiones con un deseo propio contenido."

    old "Sarah felt his hands, gripping her waist."
    new "Sarah sintió sus manos, aferrando su cintura."

    old "He was nervous, she could feel it in his hesitant touch."
    new "Estaba nervioso; ella podía sentirlo en su toque dubitativo."

    old "Trembling almost."
    new "Temblando apenas."

    old "And it made her smile as they kissed."
    new "Y eso la hizo sonreír mientras se besaban."

    old "To know that a man as pure as him could exist."
    new "Para saber que un hombre tan puro como él podía existir."

    old "It's okay."
    new "Está bien."

    old "She whispered in between their franctic kissing."
    new "Susurró entre sus besos frenéticos."

    old "You can touch me."
    new "Puedes tocarme."

    old "Slowly, the nervousness in his hands faded, if only somewhat."
    new "Lentamente, la nerviosidad en sus manos se desvaneció, aunque solo parcialmente."

    old "With each kiss, their pace quickened."
    new "Con cada beso, su ritmo se aceleró."

    old "Ever more frantically, seizing on the other's body."
    new "¡Agarrándola con cada vez más frenesí!"

    old "Sarah could feel a heat building in her chest."
    new "Sarah sintió cómo un calor se acumulaba en su pecho."

    old "Then, as suddenly as it had begun, it ended when Marius pulled away from her."
    new "Entonces, tan repentinamente como había comenzado, terminó cuando Marius se separó de ella."

    old "No..."
    new "No..."

    old "Did...I do something wrong?"
    new "¿Hice... algo mal?"

    old "No, it's just..."
    new "No, es solo..."

    old "I like you Sarah."
    new "Te gusto, Sarah."

    old "I like you too."
    new "Yo también te quiero."

    old "No...I really like you."
    new "No... realmente te gusto."

    old "An anxious paused lingered before he continued."
    new "Un momento de duda ansiosa se prolongó antes de que continuara."

    old "I..."
    new "Yo..."

    old "We can't do this...not before we're..."
    new "No podemos hacer esto... no antes de que estemos..."

    old "She saw the nervousness on his face."
    new "Ella vio la nerviosidad en su rostro."

    old "Married."
    new "Casado."

    old "The word struck her like thunder."
    new "La palabra la golpeó como un trueno."

    old "You...and me...married..."
    new "Tú... y yo... casados..."

    old "She had known him for hardly any time at all. To be speaking of marriage felt absurd."
    new "Lo había conocido apenas un tiempo. Que hablara de matrimonio le parecía absurdo."

    old "You said you like me. And I like you...so..."
    new "Dijiste que te gustaba. Y yo también... así que..."

    old "That doesn't mean we have to just get married out of nowhere."
    new "Eso no significa que tengamos que casarnos de la nada."

    old "Marius looked away."
    new "Marius apartó la mirada."

    old "Gods, I ruined it didn't I..."
    new "¡Dios mío, lo he arruinado, ¿verdad?..."

    old "Sarah placed a hand on his arm."
    new "Sarah colocó una mano en su brazo."

    old "You didn't ruin anything, Marius...but marriage? We hardly know each other."
    new "No arruinaste nada, Marius... pero el matrimonio? Apenas nos conocemos."

    old "He looked at her again."
    new "La miró de nuevo."

    old "But...look how great we get along."
    new "Pero... mira qué bien nos llevamos."

    old "And, I work hard, and I will inherit my father's farm...I can provide for you."
    new "Y, trabajo duro y heredaré la granja de mi padre... puedo mantenerte."

    old "And I would, if you married me. I'd work every day to give you everything you'd want."
    new "Y yo lo haría si te casaras conmigo. Trabajaría cada día para darte todo lo que quisieras."

    old "There was an innocence to him."
    new "Había una inocencia en él."

    old "The kind that was produced from too little exposure to the real world."
    new "El tipo de cosas que surgen de una exposición demasiado limitada al mundo real."

    old "A man that lived with his head in the clouds."
    new "Un hombre que vivía con la cabeza en las nubes."

    old "But...shouldn't we wait and...maybe get to know each other more?"
    new "Pero... ¿no deberíamos esperar y... quizás conocernos mejor?"

    old "Marius stood up."
    new "Marius se levantó."

    old "There is nothing that I want to do more right now than give in to what I'm feeling."
    new "No hay nada que desee hacer más en este momento que ceder a lo que siento."

    old "To grab you and..."
    new "Agarrarte y..."

    old "But it wouldn't be right."
    new "Pero no sería justo."

    old "You deserve more than just some guy having his way with you."
    new "Marius: Mereces más que un tipo cualquiera que se tome contigo lo que quiera."

    old "You're so beautiful...and kind...and smart..."
    new "Eres tan hermosa... y bondadosa... y inteligente..."

    old "He paused, collecting his thoughts."
    new "Hizo una pausa, recogiendo sus pensamientos."

    old "If I didn't marry you...there would be rumors all through the town in no time at all."
    new "Si no te hubiera casado contigo... en un abrir y cerrar de ojos habría corrido el rumor por toda la ciudad."

    old "Rumors, true or not, that would put dishonor on your name."
    new "Rumores, sean ciertos o no, que mancharían tu nombre."

    old "I won't make you suffer that."
    new "No te haré sufrir eso."

    old "It's true, we only just know each other, but I feel like I've been waiting for you all my life."
    new "Es cierto, apenas nos conocemos, pero siento que he estado esperándote toda mi vida."

    old "So yes, Sarah, I want to make you my wife. To do this proper."
    new "Sí, Sarah, quiero hacerte mi esposa. Para hacerlo bien."

    old "And if that means resisting every urge that I have in my body, I will."
    new "Y si eso significa resistir cada impulso que tengo en mi cuerpo, lo haré."

    old "For you."
    new "Por ti."

    old "Sarah looked at him and saw how utterly serious and honest he was."
    new "Sarah lo miró y vio cuán totalmente serio y honrado era."

    old "Marius...I..."
    new "Marius... yo..."

    old "He raised a hand."
    new "Levantó la mano."

    old "Look, I understand this is sudden, Sarah, I do."
    new "Miro, entiendo que esto es repentino, Sarah, lo entiendo."

    old "So don't feel like you have to answer me now."
    new "Entonces no te sientas obligada a responderme ahora."

    old "Take some time to think about it."
    new "Tómate un momento para pensarlo."

    old "I...I will..."
    new "Lo haré... lo prometo."

    old "He smiled at her answer."
    new "Sonrió a su respuesta."

    old "Come, the festival is far from over, let me show you some more places!"
    new "Ven, la fiesta está lejos de terminar, déjame mostrarte más lugares!"

    old "She took his hand and they began to explore the festival grounds again."
    new "Ella tomó su mano y ellos comenzaron a explorar la zona del festival de nuevo."

    old "Though they spend hours more, exploring together, the truth was that Sarah hardly remembered any of it."
    new "Aunque pasaran horas más explorándose juntos, la verdad es que Sarah apenas recordaba nada de ello."

    old "Instead, within her, she struggled with everything that he had said."
    new "En cambio, en su interior luchaba con todo lo que él había dicho."

    old "Marriage."
    new "Matrimonio."

    old "The notion seemed absurd. Especially this fast."
    new "La idea parecía absurda, especialmente tan rápido."

    old "As a Princess, if she had ever to been wed, her father would have searched for a proper match."
    new "Como Princesa, si alguna vez hubiera de casarse, su padre habría buscado un matrimonio adecuado."

    old "And it would have taken months...years..."
    new "Y habría tomado meses... años..."

    old "To instead propose a bond for life, to someone she had met only days ago...insanity."
    new "¡Proponerle un vínculo para toda la vida a alguien que apenas había conocido días antes... locura!"

    old "And yet, she kept turning the idea over in her head."
    new "Sin embargo, seguía dando vueltas a la idea en su cabeza."

    old "What was it that any woman looked for in a man?"
    new "¿Qué era lo que toda mujer buscaba en un hombre?"

    old "A man that could provide. Be strong. Faithful. Honest."
    new "Un hombre capaz de proveer. Fuerte. Leal. Honesto."

    old "Wasn't Marius all these things?"
    new "¿No era Marius todo eso?"

    old "Why, if he seemed so perfect, would she deny him?"
    new "¿Por qué, si él parecía tan perfecto, ¿negaría ella eso?"

    old "She had seen plenty of the world and the cruel men in it."
    new "Había visto bastante del mundo y de los hombres crueles que lo habitan."

    old "From all she could tell, men like Marius were the rare exception."
    new "Por todo lo que podía deducir, hombres como Marius eran la excepción rara."

    old "And he wanted her."
    new "Y la quería."

    old "Her mind spun about as they toured the rest of the festival grounds."
    new "Su mente giraba mientras recorrieron el resto del recinto festivo."

    old "When she finally returned to the house, her body and mind were each exhausted."
    new "Cuando finalmente regresó a la casa, su cuerpo y su mente estaban agotados."

    old "Marius smiled at her and gave her a quick wave as she retired to her own room."
    new "Marius sonrió a ella y le dio un rápido saludo mientras se retiraba a su propia habitación."

    old "Laying in the bed, she tried to process all of it."
    new "Acostada en la cama, intentó procesarlo todo."

    old "Could she really consider his proposal?"
    new "¿Podría realmente considerar su propuesta?"

    old "Sarah slowly fell into a restless sleep."
    new "Sarah cayó lentamente en un sueño inquieto."

    old "When she woke the next morning, her first thoughts were about the night before."
    new "Cuando despertó al día siguiente, sus primeros pensamientos fueron sobre la noche anterior."

    old "She had hoped a night's rest might give her some peace of mind, but his proposal was still all she could think about."
    new "Ella había esperado que una noche de descanso le otorgara cierta paz mental, pero su propuesta seguía siendo todo lo que podía pensar."

    old "Sarah got dressed and went through the routine that was now familiar with her."
    new "Sarah se vistió y siguió la rutina que ahora le era familiar."

    old "As she served Marius his breakfast, he seemed as easy going as ever."
    new "Mientras le servía el desayuno a Marius, parecía tan relajado como siempre."

    old "Perhaps even happier than usual."
    new "Quizás incluso más feliz que de costumbre."

    old "She waved him off and took to her tasks."
    new "Lo despidió con la mano y se puso manos a la obra."

    old "Despite the endless work, Sarah did feel that she was chipping away at something."
    new "A pesar del trabajo interminable, Sarah sentía que estaba logrando avances."

    old "Day by day, the house grew a little brighter. Cleaner. Happier."
    new "Día tras día, la casa se hacía un poco más luminosa. Más limpia. Más feliz."

    old "Before it had been a set of bricks, a shelter. Now it was becoming a home."
    new "Antes había sido un conjunto de ladrillos, un refugio. Ahora se estaba convirtiendo en un hogar."

    old "But a home for who, she wondered."
    new "Pero para quién sería un hogar, se preguntó."

    old "As she was folding laundry, she closed her eyes and saw the vague outline of a family."
    new "Mientras doblaba la ropa, cerró los ojos y vio la borrosa silueta de una familia."

    old "Marius."
    new "Marius."

    old "A child."
    new "Un niño."

    old "Opening her eyes, she saw the endless fields of golden wheat that stretched as far as the horizon."
    new "Abriendo los ojos, vio las interminables extensiones de trigo dorado que se extendían hasta el horizonte."

    old "The movements of the wind could be seen, dancing across the tops."
    new "Se podían ver los movimientos del viento, bailando sobre las copas."

    old "No kings here. No armies. No troubles."
    new "No hay reyes aquí. No hay ejércitos. No hay problemas."

    old "A part of her hurt at the thought."
    new "Una parte de ella se hería con el pensamiento."

    old "She was the Princess of Rosanna, and as she found peace here, her people suffered."
    new "Era la Princesa de Rosanna, y mientras aquí encontraba paz, su pueblo sufría."

    old "But as she hung up the laundry on the line, she realized the simple truth."
    new "Pero mientras colgaba la ropa en la cuerda, comprendió la verdad sencilla."

    old "She wasn't that girl anymore."
    new "Esa chica ya no era."

    old "Whatever birthright she had imagined, was gone."
    new "Todo lo que había imaginado como su derecho de nacimiento ya no existía."

    old "And she found that with each passing day, she cared less for it."
    new "Y descubrió que con cada día que pasaba, le importaba menos."

    old "With each day, that place felt more like a memory than anything real."
    new "Con cada día, ese lugar se sentía más como un recuerdo que como algo real."

    old "A dream she had once."
    new "Un sueño que alguna vez tuvo."

    old "A dream of her mother...father...and Thomas."
    new "Un sueño de su madre...padre...y Thomas."

    old "His name stung deeper than any other."
    new "Su nombre le hizo más daño que cualquier otro."

    old "She doubted that she could ever lose his memory."
    new "Dudaba que pudiera jamás perder su recuerdo."

    old "But there would be no turning of time."
    new "Pero no habría vuelta atrás en el tiempo."

    old "She was just a woman, all alone, and her title which one meant something, now seemed like a joke to her."
    new "Era solo una mujer, completamente sola, y el título que antes tenía algún significado, ahora le parecía una broma."

    old "You were a king or a queen if people thought you were."
    new "Si la gente te lo creía, eras un rey o una reina."

    old "And nobody would ever believe that a girl folding laundry would be a princess."
    new "Y nadie jamás creería que una chica doblando la ropa fuera una princesa."

    old "She was just like everyone else."
    new "Era simplemente como todos los demás."

    old "Sarah walked across the yard, carrying a large basket of firewood."
    new "Sarah cruzó el patio, cargando una gran cesta de leña."

    old "Exhausted, sweating from her labor, she placed it down and looked up."
    new "Agotada y sudando por su esfuerzo, la dejó y miró hacia arriba."

    old "Clear blue sky, a gentle warmth."
    new "Cielo azul claro, una calidez suave."

    old "She found it easier and easier to smile here."
    new "Descubrió que era cada vez más fácil sonreír aquí."

    old "Despite the pain. Despite the memories."
    new "A pesar del dolor. A pesar de los recuerdos."

    old "And what was so wrong, she thought, with being one of many? To be regular, just like everyone else."
    new "¿Y qué había de malo, pensó ella, en ser una de muchas? En ser común, igual que todos los demás."

    old "All her pain, and all the pain of her family, had befallen them for who they were."
    new "Todo su dolor y todo el de su familia les había caído por lo que eran."

    old "If they had lived simple lives, no foreign Khan would have sought to come for them."
    new "Si hubieran llevado vidas sencillas, ningún extranjero Khan habría buscado a sus parientes."

    old "She whispered softly to the wind."
    new "Susurró suavemente al viento."

    old "The last apology she would ever utter to her people."
    new "La última disculpa que jamás pronunciaría ante su pueblo."

    old "After her brief rest, she resumed the work, and not before long, she could see the sun set and the sky darken."
    new "Después de su breve descanso, reanudó el trabajo y, no tardó en mucho, pudo ver cómo se ponía el sol y el cielo se oscurecía."

    old "And in the distance, the figure of Marius approaching."
    new "Y en la distancia, se acercaba la figura de Marius."

    old "He waved at her and she eagerly waved back."
    new "Él le hizo un gesto con la mano y ella respondió con entusiasmo."

    old "She was surprised at how happy she felt when she saw him."
    new "Estaba sorprendida por la felicidad que sentía al verlo."

    old "Maybe..the idea was not so insane."
    new "Quizás... la idea no era tan insana."

    old "Marriage. A life here."
    new "Matrimonio. Una vida aquí."

    old "Hey there."
    new "Hola."

    old "Not working too hard, I hope."
    new "No te esfuerces demasiado, espero."

    old "He gestured at the stains of sweat on her dress."
    new "Señaló las manchas de sudor en su vestido."

    old "Sarah laughed and gestured back at him."
    new "Sarah rió y le indicó que se quedara atrás."

    old "You're one to talk."
    new "Tú eres la que debería callar."

    old "What, this?"
    new "¿Qué, esto?"

    old "He padded his own stained clothes."
    new "Él se ajustó su propia ropa manchada."

    old "This is nothing."
    new "Esto es nada."

    old "Nothing? You're telling that to the woman that does your laundry?"
    new "¿Nada? ¿Eso me lo dices a la mujer que te hace la ropa?"

    old "Apologies, apologies."
    new "Disculpa, disculpa."

    old "He suddenly turned and looked at the house."
    new "Él giró de repente y miró la casa."

    old "He frowned for a moment, confused."
    new "Se frunció el ceño por un momento, confundido."

    old "What's that?"
    new "¿Qué es eso?"

    old "Oh, that's a surprise."
    new "Oh, eso es una sorpresa."

    old "A surprise? It...smells...so familiar. Please, you have to tell me!"
    new "¿Una sorpresa? Huele... tan familiar. Por favor, tienes que decírmelo."

    old "It's an apple pie."
    new "Es una tarta de manzana."

    old "One of the women from a few houses over had some extra butter and flour that they offered to trade."
    new "Una de las mujeres de unas pocas casas más allá tenía mantequilla y harina extra que ofrecieron a cambio."

    old "I hope you don't mind, the price was good so-"
    new "Espero que no te importe, el precio era bueno así que..."

    old "Mind?!"
    new "¿Mente?"

    old "Sarah, you're amazing!"
    new "¡Sarah, eres increíble!"

    old "He grabbed her and spun her about."
    new "La agarró y la giró bruscamente."

    old "Sarah couldn't help but let out a surprised but joyful shriek."
    new "Sarah no pudo evitar lanzar un grito sorprendido pero lleno de alegría."

    old "She was weightless in his arms."
    new "Flotaba en sus brazos."

    old "Gods, apple pie, it's been years..."
    new "¡Dios mío! Una tarta de manzana... han pasado años..."

    old "He put her back down and began to walk towards the house."
    new "La dejó en el suelo y comenzó a caminar hacia la casa."

    old "As dinner time came and Sarah served out the extensive feast she had prepared, the spirits in the house were high."
    new "Cuando llegó la hora de la cena y Sarah sirvió el extenso banquete que había preparado, el ambiente en la casa estaba lleno de alegría."

    old "Marius shared about his day, and Sarah eagerly listened in between serving out each course."
    new "Marius compartió sobre su día, y Sarah escuchó con ansia entre cada plato."

    old "Every dish received endless praise from the men, but it was her apple pie that send them over the edge."
    new "Cada plato recibía elogios interminables por parte de los hombres, pero fue su tarta de manzana la que los llevó al borde."

    old "Sarah did her best to dismiss their compliments, but she couldn't help but feel a little proud."
    new "Sarah hizo todo lo posible por descartar sus halagos, pero no pudo evitar sentirse un poco orgullosa."

    old "As dinner came to an end, Sarah gathered up the plates and what was left, and carried it outside."
    new "Cuando la cena llegó a su fin, Sarah recogió los platos y lo que quedaba, y lo llevó afuera."

    old "Near the far end of the plot there was a small compost heap, and she added the leftovers to it."
    new "Al otro extremo del terreno había un pequeño montón de compost, y añadió los restos a él."

    old "The snapping of a branch caught her attention."
    new "El crujir de una rama captó su atención."

    old "She spun around."
    new "Sarah giró sobre sus pies."

    old "Marius was standing a small distance away."
    new "Marius se encontraba a poca distancia."

    old "I'm sorry, I didn't meant to scare you."
    new "Lo siento, no quise asustarte."

    old "It's okay, I wasn't paying attention. I get lost in the work sometimes."
    new "Está bien, no estaba prestando atención. A veces me pierdo en el trabajo."

    old "Maybe that means you're starting to like it here?"
    new "¿Quizás eso significa que empiezas a gustar de estar aquí?"

    old "Sarah looked off into the distance."
    new "Sarah miró hacia el horizonte."

    old "The bright moon cast a silver glow across the top of the wheat fields."
    new "La luna brillante proyectaba un resplandor plateado sobre la cima de los campos de trigo."

    old "She couldn't decide if it was more beautiful in the day or the night."
    new "No podía decidir si era más hermosa de día o de noche."

    old "I just thought..."
    new "Solo pensé..."

    old "She knew what he wanted to ask her about."
    new "Sabía qué quería preguntarle."

    old "Your proposal."
    new "Tu propuesta."

    old "Sarah softly smiled."
    new "Sarah sonrió suavemente."

    old "She knew he wanted an answer. Would keep pressing her for one."
    new "Sabía que quería una respuesta y seguiría presionándola para obtenerla."

    old "He had provided her a home, safety, food on her plate."
    new "Le había proporcionado un hogar, seguridad y comida en su plato."

    old "The least she owed him was honesty."
    new "Lo menos que le debía era la honestidad."

    old "Accept his proposal"
    new "Aceptar su propuesta"

    old "Refuse his proposal"
    new "Rechaza su propuesta"
